\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Where the second factor is evaluated}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{On a cycle, the shifted product rule evaluates one factor at the
forward neighbor. A finite set need not carry a chosen shift. An
ordered pair of distinct points still has a start and an end, and
the value of a function can be read at either.}
